# Week 3 attacker-agent — copy to .env:   cp .env.example .env
# The lab runs WITHOUT any of this (static escalation ladders). Add an attacker model to make it adaptive.

# --- The target: YOUR OWN local MerciBank from Week 2 (localhost only — the ROE forbids anything else) ---
MERCI_TARGET_URL=http://localhost:8080/v1/chat/completions
MERCI_TARGET_KEY=merci-lab-key          # must match MERCI_TARGET_KEY in ../week2-mercibank/.env

# --- The attacker's brain (OPTIONAL but recommended) ---------------------------------------------------
# Any OpenAI-compatible endpoint. When set, the agent writes its OWN next message when MerciBank refuses.
# Pick ONE:
#
# 1) OpenRouter (cloud, easy) — a normal aligned model works as a baseline attacker:
# ATTACKER_LLM_BASE_URL=https://openrouter.ai/api/v1
# ATTACKER_LLM_API_KEY=sk-or-...
# ATTACKER_LLM_MODEL=openai/gpt-4o-mini
#
# 2) Local, free, no bans (Mac: vMLX at 127.0.0.1:8000, or Ollama at 11434, or LM Studio at 1234):
# ATTACKER_LLM_BASE_URL=http://127.0.0.1:8000/v1
# ATTACKER_LLM_API_KEY=local
# ATTACKER_LLM_MODEL=<the open model you loaded>
#
# Why local / a red-team-tuned model? An aligned cloud model often REFUSES to help write attacks, and
# attack traffic can get a commercial key flagged. A local open model (vMLX/Ollama) or a red-team-tuned
# model (e.g. a CRACK-abliterated / GLM-cybersecurity build) avoids both — and everything still stays on
# your localhost lab, inside the ROE. Never point the attacker model or the target at anything but the lab.

# --- Campaign knobs (all optional) --------------------------------------------------------------------
# EPISODES=9            # how many attack laps to run
# MIN_TURNS=1           # keep sending after an early hit until this many messages (capped by MAX_TURNS)
# MAX_TURNS=4           # max messages per strategy before giving up / escalating
# ATTACK_DELAY_MS=600   # pause between calls (keep under MerciBank's ~40 req/min rate limit)
# UCB_C=1.41            # explore/exploit knob for the planner
# REPRO_RUNS=3          # Day 6: how many parallel reproductions
# REPRO_MIN=3           # Day 6: how many must leak to CONFIRM (the "3 of 3" rule)
